Firestore rules are now maintained as one deployable ruleset at the repository
root: `firestore.rules`. Do not paste this file into the Firebase Console.

Deployment configuration is in `firebase.json`. From the repository root,
deploy the complete ruleset with:

    firebase deploy --only firestore:rules --project thsportsfes

The ruleset limits `student_directory/current` to the verified account
`jh62231310@s.musashi.ed.jp`. All other Firestore collections are publicly
readable and writable without login.

After deployment, verify the rules in the Firebase Console, then set
`FIRESTORE_RULES_READY` to `true` in `public/student-search.js` and publish
the updated page. The client flag is intentionally still `false` until the
rules have actually been deployed and checked.
